{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/index.html","title":"Overview and preface","text":"Rare BooksA Vedic ConcordanceAn alphabetic index to every line of every stanza of the published Vedic literature, by Maurice Bloomfield (Harvard, 1906)Maurice Bloomfield <p>Rare Books</p> A Vedic Concordance <p>An alphabetic index to every line of every stanza of the published Vedic literature, by Maurice Bloomfield (Harvard, 1906)</p> <p>Maurice Bloomfield</p> <p>Bloomfield’s concordance of every line of the Vedic Saṃhitās, Brāhmaṇas, Āraṇyakas and Sūtras, showing where each verse recurs (Harvard Oriental Series, volume 10, 1906).</p> Start reading <p>45 chapters</p>"},{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/index.html#contents","title":"Contents","text":"<p>Chapters</p> <ul> <li>Pages 1–25</li> <li>Pages 26–50</li> <li>Pages 51–75</li> <li>Pages 76–100</li> <li>Pages 101–125</li> <li>Pages 126–150</li> <li>Pages 151–175</li> <li>Pages 176–200</li> <li>Pages 201–225</li> <li>Pages 226–250</li> <li>Pages 251–275</li> <li>Pages 276–300</li> <li>Pages 301–325</li> <li>Pages 326–350</li> <li>Pages 351–375</li> <li>Pages 376–400</li> <li>Pages 401–425</li> <li>Pages 426–450</li> <li>Pages 451–475</li> <li>Pages 476–500</li> <li>Pages 501–525</li> <li>Pages 526–550</li> <li>Pages 551–575</li> <li>Pages 576–600</li> <li>Pages 601–625</li> <li>Pages 626–650</li> <li>Pages 651–675</li> <li>Pages 676–700</li> <li>Pages 701–725</li> <li>Pages 726–750</li> <li>Pages 751–775</li> <li>Pages 776–800</li> <li>Pages 801–825</li> <li>Pages 826–850</li> <li>Pages 851–875</li> <li>Pages 876–900</li> <li>Pages 901–925</li> <li>Pages 926–950</li> <li>Pages 951–975</li> <li>Pages 976–1000</li> <li>Pages 1001–1025</li> <li>Pages 1026–1050</li> <li>Pages 1051–1075</li> <li>Pages 1076–1100</li> <li>Pages 1101–1124</li> </ul>"},{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/index.html#about-this-book","title":"About this book","text":"<p>Bloomfield’s concordance of every line of the Vedic Saṃhitās, Brāhmaṇas, Āraṇyakas and Sūtras, showing where each verse recurs (Harvard Oriental Series, volume 10, 1906). Listed in the catalogue of the Rare Book Society of India.</p> <p>From Internet Archive · Public domain in India</p><p>Scanned from a copy in the Robarts Library, University of Toronto; hosted by the Internet Archive. Item: A Vedic concordance, being an alphabetic index to every line of every stanza of the published Vedic literature and to the liturgical formulas thereof, that is an index to the Vedix Mantras, together with an account of their variations in the different Vedic books · Bloomfield, Maurice, 1855-1928 · 1906, 1124 scanned pages. Published 1906; Maurice Bloomfield died 1928; the Vedic texts are ancient; public domain in India.</p><p>This book is not stored in this library: its pages are shown from the Internet Archive when they are opened, in this library's own viewer, and each chapter ends with this credit. The pages are shown as scans in this library's viewer (zoom, pan, thumbnails); the text of this book is in a script the machine reading of the scans cannot yet give. The item on the Internet Archive (opened only if you click it).</p>"},{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/pages-1-25.html","title":"Pages 1–25","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/pages-1001-1025.html","title":"Pages 1001–1025","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/pages-101-125.html","title":"Pages 101–125","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/pages-1026-1050.html","title":"Pages 1026–1050","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/pages-1051-1075.html","title":"Pages 1051–1075","text":""},{"location":"rare-books/vedic-concordance-bloomfield/pages-1076-1100.html",